    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the number of different settings possible for a suitcase lock with 3 dials where all three digits have to be different, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the total number of possible digits on each dial. Since each dial has digits from 0 to 9, there are 10 possible digits.\n2. To ensure all three digits are different, we can select the first digit from the 10 possible digits, the second digit from the remaining 9 possible digits, and the third digit from the remaining 8 possible digits.\n\nThus, the total number of different settings possible is given by:\n\n\\[\n10 \\text{ (choices for the first digit)} \\times 9 \\text{ (choices for the second digit)} \\times 8 \\text{ (choices for the third digit)} = 10 \\times 9 \\times 8\n\\]\n\nCalculating the above product:\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 9 = 90\n\\]\n\\[\n90 \\times 8 = 720\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of different settings possible is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{720}\n\\]",
